WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.109
Host: Distinguish what ADH changes from what
aldosterone changes.

2
00:00:05.109 --> 00:00:11.467
Guide: ADH increases collecting-duct water
permeability through aquaporin-2 trafficking.

3
00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:20.830
Guide: Aldosterone enhances distal sodium
reabsorption and potassium secretion. Their
effects interact with medullary gradients,

4
00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:24.224
Guide: intake and circulating-volume signals.

5
00:00:24.224 --> 00:00:32.897
Host: ADH rises, but the medullary osmotic
gradient is greatly reduced. What limits water
recovery?

6
00:00:32.897 --> 00:00:40.745
Guide: Increased permeability still needs an
osmotic driving force. ADH makes a pathway
available;

7
00:00:40.745 --> 00:00:44.549
Guide: the medullary gradient supplies the
driving force.
